#     counts with an unreadable subfolder, the cap on 250 subfolders with 3 unreadable and 500 files in one (all listed), the cap line, and the unchanged rules (one level, hidden / system /
#     linked folders, the clash, the sync folder's failure) pass; 5 of 5 mutations of this revision are killed (Ordinal again, attempts counted, Capped on the read count, the cap line
#     without what it is on, the exact Exports not preferred). The 36 checks below were not re-run (their harness is not in the repository). Re-checked after a reboot wiped that
#     scratch: compile alone (`-t:Compile`, the project as build-app.sh step 3 makes it, no native references): 0 errors, 40 warnings with and without this patch, the same per file
#     and code; the same harness and mutations pass and are killed again.
#
# VERIFIED (2026-11-20, M1 Pro)
#   * Compile: a copy of the generated device project (gameapp.csproj, sources re-pointed to the copy, GameAppSlot.cs and GameAppSlotUi.cs added, the project's own GameAppExport.cs and
#     GameAppBuild.cs kept), `dotnet build gameapp.csproj -c Release -r ios-arm64 -t:Compile -nologo`: the 0076 tree rc 0, 0 errors, 40 warnings; with this patch rc 0, 0 errors, 40 warnings,
#     the same warnings per file and code (none in GameAppNas.cs). No .ipa was made.
#   * Host check of the pure part (GameAppNas.cs with NAS_LOGIC_ONLY, GameAppCloud.cs, GameAppUi.cs, GameAppCover.cs, net11.0, a fake lister): 36 of 36 checks (the owner's layout: the South
#     Park game two levels down not listed and its inner folder never listed; real Remote paths and sizes; hidden, system, linked folders and Exports never listed as game folders; Exports
#     .ipa only; .part, "._" and .ipa files of a subfolder skipped; an unreadable subfolder skipped and named; one list call per folder; the clash rule (top level first, then folders by
#     name) and its log lines, capped at 10; the 200 cap on 250 folders (first 200 by name, 201 calls, logged); the summary line; CloudOnlyGames shows the subfolder's base game and not its
#     update / DLC; DownloadSet gives base + update + DLC with their subfolder paths, minus what Documents has; the cached list round-trips the paths; the sync folder's own failure throws).
#     8 of 8 mutations killed (links followed, no cap, last of a name wins, hidden folders listed, .ipa kept in subfolders, Exports listed as a game folder, a subfolder's failure fatal,
#     subfolders unsorted).
#
# NOT VERIFIED
#   * Nothing ran on an iPhone, in the simulator, or against an SFTP server: SSH.NET's ListDirectory attributes (IsSymbolicLink for a link to a folder, FullName as an absolute path) are
#     read from its API, not observed on the owner's NAS.
#   * Time of a refresh with many subfolders over the owner's network (one round trip per subfolder, up to 200) is not measured.
#   * A 200-row action sheet in BrowseNas is not looked at on a phone.
#   * A file in a subfolder that has the name of a file of ANOTHER source (a Files folder) is not a clash here: CloudOnlyGames keeps the first source, as before.
#   * The sync folder's own files still accept a link and a "._" name, as before (TopFile is unchanged on purpose).
